#=GF RL   Genomics Proteomics Bioinformatics. 2007;5:187-195.
#=GF CC   Animal histone pre-mRNAs are spliced by a different mechanism than nuclear
#=GF CC   pre-mRNAs and self-splicing introns. This processing involves the U7
#=GF CC   snRNP, which contains only one RNA species: U7. The 5' end of U7 RNA is
#=GF CC   thought to base-pair to a conserved spacer element downstream of the
#=GF CC   cleavage site in histone pre-mRNA. This family contains a number of
#=GF CC   annotated U7 pseudogenes.
